From 0767422fb116fe870f7d2dc945273e0bca5e5aaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: indextree <hellonypcteam@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:45:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] Fix python verifier; share the rust transcript

- verify(circuit, output, input, proof): initial claim is D~(z0) of the
  caller's claimed output with z0 from the transcript (upstream took D and z0
  from the proof and never compared D with anything)
- sumcheck: exact round count (upstream v == 1 early accept), exact degree
  bound, challenges recomputed from a chained transcript, and the final value
  g_v(r_v) is bound to add~/mult~ of the verifier's circuit (upstream compared
  against prover-supplied f[i] and used prover-supplied add/mult/k)
- z_{i+1} = l(b*, c*, r*) recomputed, final claim checked against the caller's
  input MLE (upstream used prover-supplied input_func and z)
- transcript.py: circomlib-compatible MiMC7 transcript identical to rust
  (upstream used ethsnarks mimc_hash, which is a different MiMC than circom's)
- test_security.py: KATs shared with rust, identical proofs, tampering, and a
  concrete forgery accepted by the verbatim upstream verifier (legacy_upstream.py)
